WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 0.3 · Start Here: Your Founder Journey
Baseline health check of your foundations

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Rate each foundation honestly today; most will be not started, and that is fine.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.393
A health check is a short self-assessment of how developed each foundation of your initiative is today. It is not a test and there is no passing score: it makes your starting point visible.

4
00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:28.393
The ratings, shown for finance

5
00:00:28.393 --> 00:00:36.389
Not started: Nothing exists yet. For example: No budget; one founder pays for flour personally and keeps receipts in a drawer.

6
00:00:36.389 --> 00:00:47.719
Informal: It happens, but it lives in one person’s head or habits. For example: One founder tracks the stall’s takings in a personal notebook that nobody else can read.

7
00:00:47.719 --> 00:00:57.937
Documented: It is written down, though perhaps rarely opened. For example: A first-year budget of about US$48,000 and a one-page note on who can spend what.

8
00:00:57.937 --> 00:01:10.467
Practised, then reviewed: People actually use it; then you check whether it works and improve it. For example: Both co-founders approve larger payments, and lowered the limit after a near miss.

9
00:01:10.867 --> 00:01:11.467
Why it matters

10
00:01:11.467 --> 00:01:17.141
1. Most areas start not started or informal, and that is expected.

11
00:01:17.141 --> 00:01:21.704
2. Seeing the gaps helps you choose your priorities.

12
00:01:21.704 --> 00:01:28.378
3. At the end, you compare and see what you have built.

13
00:01:28.778 --> 00:01:29.378
How you will use it

14
00:01:29.378 --> 00:01:34.681
1. Pick three priorities for this course from your weakest areas.

15
00:01:34.681 --> 00:01:39.985
2. Share it with a co-founder or mentor and discuss differences.

16
00:01:39.985 --> 00:01:45.919
3. Repeat it after Module 10 and compare with today.

17
00:01:46.319 --> 00:01:46.919
What to avoid

18
00:01:46.919 --> 00:01:51.111
Generous ratings with no evidence behind them.

19
00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:54.563
Writing documents that nobody practises.

20
00:01:54.563 --> 00:02:00.867
Rating alone when a second view would show blind spots.

21
00:02:01.467 --> 00:02:03.267
You rate each area, give evidence and name three priorities.

22
00:02:03.267 --> 00:02:07.267
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:08.767 --> 00:02:11.867
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
